<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cursim</span></b> , adv.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>quickly, swiftly, hastily, speedily</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">currere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 3, 124</span></i>
			; Afran. ap. <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 186</span></i> P.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc cito et cursim est agendum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 3, 1, 64</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rapi ad carnuficem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 2, 156</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agmine acto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 16, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicere aliena (opp. sensim dicere quod causae
					prodesset),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 2, 17, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arripere aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 2, 89, 364</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pergere ad aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 5, 5, 13</span></i>
			 et saep.</div>
